from __future__ import annotations

from site_assets import THINKING_PANEL_URI, PANEL_DIALOGUE_URI, LINKEDIN, MEDIUM
from site_components import nav, footer, opportunity, THOUGHTS, thought_grid


def thinking() -> str:
    return f'''{nav("thinking")}<main><section class="pagehero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Selected thinking</p><h1>Writing about the decisions that make enterprise AI usable.</h1><p>I use writing to work through practical leadership questions I have encountered in enterprise settings: where value gets lost, what governance should actually do, how operating models shape behavior, why data readiness matters and what has to change for adoption to become part of everyday work.</p></div></section><section class="section paper"><div class="container"><div class="head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Leading in the AI Enterprise</p><h2>A small selection shaped by recurring operating questions.</h2></div><p>This is intentionally curated rather than a complete archive. The common thread is the judgment required to move from promising AI activity toward repeatable enterprise capability.</p></div>{thought_grid(THOUGHTS,"articles")}<div class="actions"><a class="btn dark" href="{MEDIUM}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-hq-event="medium_thinking">More writing on Medium ↗</a><a class="btn dark" href="{LINKEDIN}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-hq-event="linkedin_thinking">LinkedIn ↗</a></div></div></section><section class="section white"><div class="container editorial-split"><div><p class="eyebrow">How I use writing</p><h2>A point of view is useful only when it improves a decision.</h2><p>I am not interested in publishing for volume. The strongest pieces start from tensions I have seen in enterprise work and force me to take a position I would be willing to defend with a leadership team.</p><div class="grid3" style="margin-top:24px"><article class="card"><span class="org">Experience first</span><h3>Start from a real operating tension</h3><p>Governance versus speed, experimentation versus scale, centralized expertise versus business ownership, or technical possibility versus adoption. These tensions produce better thinking than trend summaries.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="org">Judgment</span><h3>State the trade-off clearly</h3><p>Most enterprise decisions are not solved by a universal best practice. I try to explain what changes the answer, what evidence matters and which compromise I would choose in a given context.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="org">Practical use</span><h3>Leave the reader with a better question</h3><p>Useful writing should help a leader frame the problem differently, challenge an assumption or make the next decision with more precision. If it does not change the conversation, it is mostly content.</p></article></div></div><div class="editorial-photo portrait"><img src="{THINKING_PANEL_URI}" alt="Jair Ribeiro listening during an industry panel discussion" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div></section><section class="section paper"><div class="container speak"><img src="{PANEL_DIALOGUE_URI}" alt="Jair Ribeiro contributing to a conference panel discussion" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div><p class="eyebrow">External context</p><h2>Writing, speaking and research are supporting evidence, not the identity.</h2><p>The same questions appear in practice, research and executive conversations. Writing and speaking give me another way to test whether an argument remains useful outside the context in which it was formed.</p><div class="prooflist"><div class="proofitem"><strong>Thinkers360</strong> — Top 50 Global Thought Leaders &amp; Influencers on Emerging Technology (2023), treated as external recognition rather than a professional title.</div><div class="proofitem"><strong>Generative AI Summit 2023, London</strong> — keynote on scaling AI adoption across the enterprise.</div><div class="proofitem"><strong>Research focus</strong> — MSc work on Responsible AI adoption in global enterprises.</div></div></div></div></section>{opportunity()}</main>{footer()}'''
